==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Great damage.
* A somewhat large hitbox.
* Great combo potential.
* Fast moves with low endlag.
* Fast M1, making it good for raids and grinding.
* All moves can hit [[Sea Beast]]s.
* Long range moves.
* Good AoE.

|'''[Z] Swords Dance'''
* Fast mobility move.
* Good for PvP on water (If the user does not use [[Shark]]).
* Can grab the target(s) regardless of if they have [[Instinct]] or not.
* Decent knockback.
* Great cooldown.
* One of the few moves which can stun [[Blade]] users, along with [[Rengoku]].

|'''[X] True Air Slash'''
* Long range.
* Decent knockback.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Cannot deal damage to [[Blade]] users, but {{Ability|Z}} can stun them.
* Dashes on the fourth swing, making it harder to farm with.
* Both skills can be dodged with [[Instinct]].
* High mastery requirements for players below [[Third Sea]].

|'''[Z] Swords Dance'''
* Travel distance is very short, requiring it to land if the target is close.
* Easy to [[Instinct]] trick.

|'''[X] True Air Slash'''
* Easy to dodge.
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* Saishi, along with [[Shizu]] and [[Oroshi]] are required (and with 300 [[mastery]] on each respectively) to obtain the [[True Triple Katana]].
* The user can grab [[Love]]'s {{Ability|Love|V}} with {{Ability|Z}}.
* Saishi is debated to be the best [[sword]] in the [[Second Sea]], with its main competitors being [[Rengoku]], [[Dragon Trident]], and [[Midnight Blade]].
* {{Ability|Z}} will lock the user in place for a second after dealing damage to big targets such as [[Sea Beast]]s.
* {{Ability|Z}} and {{Ability|X}} deal the same amount of damage. (Only if {{Ability|Z}} is used close to the target)
* Saishi and the other [[True Triple Katana]] [[Swords]] were once had different names Saishi/Saddi.
